# The Acid steps page (the ARP button's fifth page, after Acid answer): a white key chooses a step of the acid line; the knobs set its kind (rest, note, accent,
# slide, accent and slide), its note (scale steps above the chord) and its octave; Frozen holds the line (an edit freezes it) and stores it with the piece.
seed 0
wait 3000
turn SELECT 13 100
expect view 13
expect par173 0
# step 3 (the third white key, key 4): an accent, five scale steps up, two octaves up
tapkey 4
spin K1 -10
wait 100
expect acidkind2 0
spin K1 2
wait 100
expect acidkind2 2
spin K2 -20
spin K2 5
wait 100
expect acidoff2 5
spin K3 -5
spin K3 2
wait 100
expect acidoct2 2
# an edit froze the line
expect par173 1
shot acsteps.png
# stored with the piece, and back after a power cycle
tap GLO
tap SAVE
wait 500
reboot
wait 500
expect par173 1
expect acidkind2 2
expect acidoff2 5
expect acidoct2 2
# frozen: it does not change (Mutate at the top, ten seconds on)
turn SELECT 11 100
expect view 11
spin K4 100
wait 10000
expect acidkind2 2
expect acidoff2 5
